WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.930
Settle into a position you can leave or change whenever you need.

2
00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:18.480
Let your eyes close only if that feels comfortable; otherwise keep a soft, steady view of the space in front of you.

3
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:25.830
Feel the surface beneath you doing some of the work of holding you.

4
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.200
There is no ideal breath to find.

5
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:43.705
Notice the breath that is already happening.

6
00:00:45.405 --> 00:00:54.195
It may be long or short, smooth or uneven, easy to feel or barely noticeable.

7
00:00:55.895 --> 00:00:59.670
Let it keep its own pace.

8
00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:11.469
Choose one place where breathing is reasonably clear.

9
00:01:13.169 --> 00:01:22.284
You might feel air passing at the nostrils, movement across the chest, or a gentle change around the belly.

10
00:01:23.984 --> 00:01:28.869
Stay with just one inhale, from its beginning until it turns.

11
00:01:37.449 --> 00:01:39.729
Then meet one exhale.

12
00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:44.744
You do not need to extend it.

13
00:01:46.444 --> 00:01:54.699
Notice how it begins, how it moves, and how it comes to an end by itself.

14
00:02:03.278 --> 00:02:07.613
Now receive the next breath in the same way.

15
00:02:09.313 --> 00:02:10.353
One inhale.

16
00:02:12.053 --> 00:02:13.613
One exhale.

17
00:02:15.313 --> 00:02:19.543
This breath does not have to resemble the one before it.

18
00:02:30.268 --> 00:02:31.708
Attention will leave.

19
00:02:33.408 --> 00:02:38.353
You may hear a sound, follow a thought, or begin planning.

20
00:02:40.053 --> 00:02:44.943
When you notice, there is no need to review where you went.

21
00:02:46.643 --> 00:02:51.648
Feel the support beneath you, and meet the breath that is here now.

22
00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:13.157
If attending to breathing feels uncomfortable, move attention to your hands or feet instead.

23
00:03:14.857 --> 00:03:19.162
Notice pressure, temperature, or contact.

24
00:03:20.862 --> 00:03:30.112
You can let the breath remain in the background and continue with one clear sensation at a time.

25
00:03:40.836 --> 00:03:50.456
For the next few breaths, use a few quiet words if they help: arriving as you breathe in, releasing as you breathe out.

26
00:03:52.156 --> 00:03:55.841
Or leave the breath without a label.

27
00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:15.356
Notice that you have not needed to hold every breath in mind.

28
00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:22.050
You have only been asked to meet the current one.

29
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:28.880
The practice begins again each time attention returns.

30
00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:42.985
Let awareness widen to include the whole body and the room.

31
00:04:44.685 --> 00:04:49.160
Notice light, sound, and the next movement you want to make.

32
00:04:50.860 --> 00:05:00.000
Take this simple rhythm with you: not every breath, only the one that is here.
